[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to the replacement lens kit tutorial. In just six simple steps, learn how to replace your lenses yourself. The kit includes interchangeable lenses,'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a lens removal tool, a lens storage case, a prying tool, an air blower, a soft brush, disposable gloves, cleaning wipes, a lens cloth, and a guide. Make sure you change your lenses in a clean,'

[00:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dry indoor environment with humidity below 60% to prevent lens fogging or dust from entering. If humidity is high, use the air conditioner\'s dehumidification mode. We\'ll use one lens as an example for the'

[00:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'process. Hold the drone or place it on a flat, clean surface. Align the red mark on the lens removal'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tool with the white mark on the lens retention ring. Rotate counterclockwise until the ring loosens.'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then lift the tool to remove it. Insert the pry tool along the edge of'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the old lens and lift it off. Inspect the inner lens for dust or'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stains that may affect image quality. Use compressed air to remove surface dust.'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Brush off any remaining particles. Wipe in circular motions with a cleaning wipe.'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Finish by cleaning with a lens cloth. Open the lens storage case. Use the'

[02:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'suction cup to remove the new lens. Align it with the inner lens and attach it to the drone body. Align the ring with the drone body and'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rotate clockwise about four full turns. Finally, remove the suction cup to'

[03:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'complete installation. After replacing the lenses, perform stitching correction to prevent image misalignment.'

[03:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Before starting, confirm the following. One, lenses are properly installed. Two, no propeller guards are attached to'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the drone. Three, battery levels meet the following requirements. Drone above 70%. Goggles above 30%.'

[03:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Controller above 30%. Open the vision goggles menu in an outdoor environment. Head to stitching correction in the shooting menu as shown'

[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and tap start correction. Environmental requirements. Choose a bright, open, and calm area with no obstructions. Keep tall objects such as'

[04:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'trees or buildings at least 150 m away. Recommended altitude 30 to 70 m. Once in position, maintain a stable'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hover without moving or rotating the drone. Press and hold C1 to begin. The drone will automatically perform its calibration. If calibration fails, confirm that all conditions are met.'

[04:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Adjust as needed and retry. Thank you for watching.'
